    feat: add hiragana/katakana prompt script selection
    
    Practice and Arcade share a script setting via FilterContext. The selector
    changes what the prompt renders only — input stays romaji and the typing
    engine keeps matching the underlying hiragana, so useTypingEngine and
    game/engine are untouched.
    
    - displayFor(kana, script) in kanaGroups owns the transform, reusing
      wanakana's toKatakana
    - TypingCanvas routes both the token row and the composed-kana preview
      through that one seam; KanaToken's memo comparator now keys on the
      rendered string so a script switch is not memoised stale
    - ArcadePage maps its pool's kana through displayFor, leaving romajiTarget
      alone, so the shared selector is not a control that does nothing
    - fix: DEFAULT_GROUPS referenced 's-line', which matches no group id, so
      the sa-so row silently never appeared in the default round
    
    Also documents the project's two game modes and the shared spine in
    CLAUDE.md, with PLAN.md covering the unstarted Tatoeba sentence mode.
    
